---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const eventMeanings = [
  ['triage_click', 'A click on a triage booking link; not proof of a booking.'],
  ['mailto_click', 'A click on an email link; not proof that an email was sent.'],
  ['scope_generated', 'A locally generated scope brief; the brief content is not a counter event field.'],
  ['pilot_click', 'A click on a pilot link; not proof of a sale or payment.']
];
---

<Layout title="Site Data & Event Counter Disclosure — BitEvo" description="A bounded disclosure of BitEvo public-site event-counter fields, disabled status, and unresolved provider retention boundaries." robots="noindex, follow" alternates={{ en: '/privacy', ru: '/ru/privacy' }}>
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Site data · limited disclosure</div>
        <h1 class="display">What an event would mean, and what it would not prove.</h1>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">As of 13 October 2026, the BitEvo first-party event counter is OFF. This page describes the reviewed but inactive event model. It does not claim live analytics collection, a verified production database, or a complete legal privacy policy.</p>
        <p>Any future activation requires separate review of the disclosure, provider configuration, retention and evidence of correct counting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div class="container boundary-grid">
      <article class="panel">
        <div class="eyebrow">Current state</div>
        <h2>Counting disabled</h2>
        <p>The public event-counter bootstrap is disabled, and the event receiver and report endpoints fail closed. A listed event is not evidence that it was recorded in a live database.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <div class="eyebrow">Scope of this notice</div>
        <h2>Aggregate events only</h2>
        <p>This is a bounded event-counter disclosure, not a statement that hosting providers create no logs. Scope-request handling and engagement evidence have separate boundaries.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Proposed event model · currently OFF</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">What the counter table is designed to contain</h2>
      <p>When the BitEvo first-party event counter is activated, it counts clicks on triage booking links, email links and pilot links, as well as local scope-brief generation. Only the date, event type, page, language and aggregate count are stored in the counter table. Contact details, form or scope-brief contents, cookies and IP addresses are not stored in that table. A recorded event does not confirm that an email was sent, an appointment was booked or a service was purchased.</p>
      <p>The browser counter payload is limited to <code>event</code>, <code>page</code> and <code>locale</code>. The server may transiently derive a keyed IP token for rate limiting, but the counter's aggregate table has no token or request-ID column. This does not rule out infrastructure-level processing by hosting or security providers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-rule">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Event meanings</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">An interaction is not a conversion.</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        {eventMeanings.map(([event, meaning]) => (
          <article class="panel"><h3><code>{event}</code></h3><p>{meaning}</p></article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Unresolved before activation</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Retention and provider logs need separate verification.</h2>
      <p>No retention period for event aggregates is approved by this page. Infrastructure logs may be processed by Vercel, Cloudflare or other relevant providers; their retention, access and deletion boundaries have not been established here. Do not infer that all provider logs are absent.</p>
      <p>For the separately stated 30-day scope-request retention boundary and engagement-specific evidence rules, see <a href="/security">Security & Data Handling</a>. That period is not an event-counter retention rule.</p>
      <p>Questions about BitEvo's public-site handling can be addressed to <a href="mailto:robert@bitevo.work">robert@bitevo.work</a>. The public intake must not be used to submit credentials or production secrets.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
